# Dual Git remotes

This repository is mirrored to two remotes:

- `origin`: `https://github.com/ahmadubuntu/kafka_administration.git`
- `azure`: `https://azure.charisma.tech/DataPlatform/DataPlatform/_git/kafka_administration`

Keep `main` tracking `origin/main`. After pushing a release or commit to
GitHub, mirror the branch and tags to Azure.

Use `AZDO_PAT_DATAPLATFORM` for Azure authentication. Never use `AZDO_PAT`,
print the token, commit it, or embed it in a remote URL.

```bash
AUTH_HEADER="AUTHORIZATION: Basic $(printf ':%s' "$AZDO_PAT_DATAPLATFORM" | base64 -w0)"
git -c credential.helper= -c http.extraHeader="$AUTH_HEADER" push azure main
git -c credential.helper= -c http.extraHeader="$AUTH_HEADER" push azure --tags
git branch --set-upstream-to=origin/main main
```

For read-only verification:

```bash
AUTH_HEADER="AUTHORIZATION: Basic $(printf ':%s' "$AZDO_PAT_DATAPLATFORM" | base64 -w0)"
git -c credential.helper= -c http.extraHeader="$AUTH_HEADER" ls-remote azure
```
